            <ArticleTitle>Acute profound thrombocytopenia with second exposure to eptifibatide associated with a strong antibody reaction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>64-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/09537100802592676</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of eptifibatide-induced acute profound thrombocytopenia in a 64-year-old male receiving eptifibatide for the second time during percutaneous coronary intervention. Although rare, short and self-limited episodes of acute and profound thrombocytopenia have been associated with eptifibatide exposure. The thrombocytopenia is thought to be immune mediated, and assays are available to test for eptifibatide-induced platelet antibodies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
